    {
      "id": "b9fe78b1-de4c-4908-b240-cc0516984943",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### Method examination task\n\nThe next cell contains the `generateColor` method. Examine that method and then edit this cell to answer the questions. \n\n1. Identify the following based on the method signature.\n    * visibility modifier: \n    * return type: \n    * method identifier: \n    * parameter list: \n2. `gNumber` is a `String` object and we can ask it to run `String` methods. We use one of those methods in the `generateColor` method.\n    * What is the identifier of that `String` method?\n    * How many arguments does it have?\n3. The `generateColor` method also uses a method of the `Integer` class.\n    * What is the identifier of that method? \n    * How many arguments does it have?\n\nNow run the next *three* code cells to display a color based on your G number.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "b9fe78b1-de4c-4908-b240-cc0516984943"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3368e9a3-bffe-41aa-b5e0-5d7b4a6ca878",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// Not magic code because you've seen examples like this code in the activities\n// But don't change it unless directed to do so\n\npublic Color generateColor(String gNumber) {\n    String redChars = gNumber.substring(3, 5);\n    String greenChars = gNumber.substring(5, 7);\n    String blueChars = gNumber.substring(7, 9);\n    \n    int red = Integer.parseInt(redChars);\n    int green = Integer.parseInt(greenChars);\n    int blue = Integer.parseInt(blueChars);\n\n    red = red * 2 + 37;\n    green = green * 2 + 46;\n    blue = blue * 2 + 12;\n\n    Color colorResult = new Color(red, green, blue);\n    return colorResult;\n}",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "d3876702-ae2c-4aaf-90b9-8007911cc6c6",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "Color myColor = generateColor(gNumber);\nSystem.out.println(\"Color generated from gNumber: \" + myColor);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "e7714ce7-5f7c-4cb4-8be4-546f261170aa",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// Magic code to display a small square with a specified color. Do not change this code.\n\nimport javax.swing.JFrame;\nimport javax.swing.JPanel;\nimport javax.swing.JLabel;\nimport javax.swing.SwingConstants;\nimport java.awt.Dimension;\nimport java.awt.Font;\n\nJFrame frame = new JFrame(\"Color Display\");\nJPanel panel = new JPanel();\npanel.setPreferredSize(new Dimension(625, 225));\nJLabel colorLabel = new JLabel(\"\");\ncolorLabel.setPreferredSize(new Dimension(200, 200));\ncolorLabel.setOpaque(true);\ncolorLabel.setBackground(myColor);\npanel.add(colorLabel);\nframe.add(panel);\nframe.pack();\nframe.setVisible(true);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "e4a9d162-016c-49b9-9749-b8598ccaeee7",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### Color and text display task\n\nIn the magic code, one new kind of object we used has the type `JLabel`. A `JLabel` object can display a line of text in different fonts and sizes, and we can change both the color of the text and the background color by asking the object to invoke specific methods.\n\nHere are the lines that that use `JLabel` methods change the properties of the object that has the identifier `colorLabel`.\n\n```java\ncolorLabel.setPreferredSize(new Dimension(200, 200));\ncolorLabel.setOpaque(true);\ncolorLabel.setBackground(myColor);\n```\n\nEdit the following descriptive cell to answer questions about this code\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "e4a9d162-016c-49b9-9749-b8598ccaeee7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ab407da8-30ee-4221-9113-f5ff47ff151b",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "1. What are the identifiers for three methods that we ask the `colorLabel` object to invoke?\n2. In the first line, if you changed `200, 200` to `300, 300`, what do you think will happen?\n3. What does \"opaque\" mean? Based on that, what is the purpose of the second line?",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "ab407da8-30ee-4221-9113-f5ff47ff151b"
      }
    },
    {
