      "id": "00f2928c-7548-491f-945c-b825feb4f593",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### Text display task\n\nEvery `JLabel` object has a `setText` method for changing the text. The signature for that method is\n```java\npublic void setText(String text)\n```\n\nIdentify the following for the `setText` method.\n* Visibility modifier\n* Return type\n* Method identifier\n* Parameter list\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "00f2928c-7548-491f-945c-b825feb4f593"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "776f76d0-926f-4455-9ee9-ce2bc4425a83",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "When a method has the return type `void`, we expect the method to do something, but it won't return any information to whoever invoked it. So we expect the `setText` method to change the text in the `JLabel` object, but not tell us anything else.\n\nRun the following code cell to see the effect of the `setText` method on the `colorLabel` object. (And we'll see how to modify the properties of this text later.)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "776f76d0-926f-4455-9ee9-ce2bc4425a83"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "37b3ae16-af30-4872-be64-580f2b9fc3e0",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "colorLabel.setText(fullName);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
