      "source": "// Magic code: Do not change the following line\n\nJLabel secondColorLabel = new JLabel(\"\");\n\n// Your work starts below this line.\n// Add one line that declares a new String variable for a different G number. \n// Use any identifier you want, and assign it a G number value\n// different than any of those above.\n\n\n\n// Add one line that declares a new Color variable with any identifier you want. \n// Assign it the result of using the method generateColor\n// with the G number variable you just defined as an argument.\n\n\n\n// Following the example in previous cells, add lines that do the following.\n// 1. Change the size of the secondColorLabel object to any size you choose.\n// 2. Make the object opaque\n// 3. Sets the color to the one you just defined.\n\n\n\n// Run the cells from the beginning after this step to see the results. Then, continue\n// to the next step in this cell.\n\n\n// Declare a new String variable with any identifier you want. Assign it a value of a different full name.\n\n\n// Add one line that sets the text of the secondColorLabel to the new full name variable you just defined.\n\n\n// magic code to display the new color label. Do not change this code.\npanel.add(secondColorLabel);\nframe.pack();\n\n",
