      "id": "3f4228c0-6cb8-4bf7-93a0-2be05bb4fa50",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### Text alignment task\n\nWe'll now practice taking a description of a method and applying it in our code. In this case, we want to align the text in the `JLabel` object in different ways.\n\n`JLabel` has two methods that can do that: `setHorizontalAlignment` and `setVerticalAlignment`. Those methods each take one argument.\n\nFor `setHorizontalAlignment`, that argument must be one of the following.\n\n```java\nSwingConstants.LEFT\nSwingConstants.CENTER\nSwingConstants.RIGHT\n```\n\nFor `setVerticalAlignment`, that argument must be one of the following.\n\n```java\nSwingConstants.TOP\nSwingConstants.CENTER\nSwingConstants.BOTTOM\n```\n\nIn the next code cell, add four lines of code that invoke these methods to align the text in each `JLabel` object in a different way.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "3f4228c0-6cb8-4bf7-93a0-2be05bb4fa50"
      }
